Polymorphism
    Poly -> Many
    morphism -> forms
a. static polymorphism   -> eg: Method overloading, Method Hiding
b. dynamic polymorphism  -> eg: Method overriding

Method-overloading
Two methods is said to be overloaded, iff both the methods have same name but different argument types
In case of method-overloading, Compiler will bind the call of the method to the body of method.
JVM should just execute the method body, so we say Method-overloading as "CompileTimeBinding/EarlyBinding".

                    implicit-TypeCasting

byte ⇨ short ↘️
                int ⇨ long ⇨ float ⇨ double
         char ↗️

⇦ ─────────────────────────────────────
                    explicit-TypeCasting


Overloading

Compiler binding the call based on argument
    a. if exact match is found bind the call
    b. if exact match not found, perform
       implicit typecasting till it reaches to bind
    c. upon implicit typecasting still if the call
       can't be bind, it would result in "CE"

---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------

Overriding
During inheritance, the parent class method implementation would not match the needs of the child class
so child class will take the method name, but it will change the implementation as per the needs of the child class.

In case of overriding, JVM will bind the method calls based on the runtime object, but not on the reference type so
we say overriding has "TruePolymorphism/LateBinding/RuntimeBinding"

Rules of Overriding
1 In case of overriding, we can't change the return-type of the method, if we want to change then
 there should be relationship bow return-type of the methods
2 while overriding, we_can't reduce the scope of access modifier.
        private< default < protected < public